--- !u!114 &5968524885506049006
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 4617429315361063015}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 3a267081e25f0694a8aac637c7906929, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  rootNode:
    dialogueText: 'Ah, young one! I have a story for you. A lesson about honesty
      and responsibility. Would you like to hear it?

'
    playerChoices:
    - Yes! I love stories!
    - Why should I listen to this?
    - Maybe later...
    npcResponses:
    - Village Chief smiles and begins.
    - Because knowledge is the greatest treasure.
    - Come back when you are ready.
    nextNodes:
    - dialogueText: "There was once a boy named Lio who loved playing tricks. One
        day, he ran into the village shouting, \u2018Fire! Fire! The fields are burning!"
      playerChoices:
      - 
      - 
      - 
      npcResponses:
      - 
      - 
      - 
      nextNodes:
      - dialogueText: 'The villagers rushed with buckets of water, but there was
          no fire. Lio laughed, thinking it was funny.



          The next day,
          he did it again. The villagers were angry, but they forgave him.'
        playerChoices:
        - 
        - 
        - 
        npcResponses:
        - 
        - 
        - 
        nextNodes:
        - dialogueText: "Then, on the third day, a real fire broke out! Lio screamed
            for help\u2026 but no one believed him. By the time they realized the
            truth, the fire had already spread."
          playerChoices:
          - So, what happened to Lio?
          - "Why didn\u2019t the villagers check anyway?"
          - He should have lied better
          npcResponses:
          - He learned his lesson, but at great cost
          - Trust, once broken, is hard to fix
          - Lies will always come back to hurt you
          nextNodes:
          - dialogueText: 'Moral of this Story is

              Honesty is like
              a strong bridge. If you weaken it with lies, it will collapse when
              you need it most. Always speak the truth, for truth builds trust'
            playerChoices:
            - 
            - 
            - 
            npcResponses:
            - 
            - 
            - 
            nextNodes:
